# Every third-party package a leaf script imports, including the heavy ones
# requirements.in leaves out, so one CI job can run every script rather than
# skip three of them. That skip is how a traceback in the feature-store skew
# script went unnoticed: nothing ever started it with its dependency present.
#
# mlflow-skinny provides the `mlflow` module the promotion gate imports without
# the tracking server's web stack; readers install `mlflow` as their leaf says.
# azure-identity is present so the keyless paths are exercised as well as the
# fallbacks that run without it.
#
# Regenerate the pinned, hashed lockfile after editing, from this directory,
# for the runner's Python (ubuntu-latest):
#   uv pip compile --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-full.txt requirements-full.in
-r requirements.in
mlflow-skinny
feast
pandas
langgraph
azure-identity
